  biomeName: The Static Matrix
  minDepthMeters: 14000
  maxDepthMeters: 15000
  shortDescription: Stone compressed until it resembles a digital grid.
  isPlaceholder: 0
  visitPurpose: Late-game pressure biome. Come here only for major progress, rare
    extraction, and to keep orientation in soft terrain and hunt hidden value.
  commonRewardHook: Even routine value here comes from Nickel Ore and Cobalt Alloy.
  rareRewardHook: 'The reason to risk the trip is: Abyssal Crystal and High-Capacity
    Cell.'
  landmarkIdentity: The Static Matrix reads through dunes, plains, void cuts, and
    shape changes in the floor. Landmarks should feel singular and intimidating.
  safePocketIdentity: Safe pockets are rare and temporary. Retreat routes matter
    more than comfort.
  riskSummary: 'Main failure mode: orientation loss and long empty recovery swims,
    depth stress, and expensive hesitation. Creature pressure stays high.'
  extractionFocus: 'Exact deep extraction with little tolerance for wasted movement.
    Deep tier: accept longer sweeps and weaker orientation during gathering, extract
    only what justifies the risk, and leave cleanly.'
  landmarkGuidance: Dominant landmark is iron shard ridge or compressed metal plain
    break. This slot should read through cold industrial skyline made by geology;
    use silhouette changes to avoid getting lost in soft terrain.
